  "text": "Viral Genome\nMutation Predictor\nYou are a bio-informatics engineer tasked with synthesizing a safe DNA sequence of length \n (composed\nof characters 'A', 'C', 'G', 'T'). However, there are \n forbidden viral mutation signatures (strings). A DNA\nsequence is considered \"safe\" if it does not contain ANY of the forbidden viral signatures as a substring.\nSince the number of valid sequences can be incredibly large, output the result modulo \n.\nInput Format\nThe first line contains two integers \n (number of forbidden signatures) and \n (length of the target DNA\nsequence) The next \n lines each contain a string representing a forbidden viral signature.\nConstraints\n (Note: \n is extremely large!)\n length of each forbidden string \nStrings\nconsist only of the characters 'A', 'C', 'G', 'T'.\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer: the number of safe DNA sequences of length \n modulo \n.\nSample Input 0\n2 3\nAC\nCG\nSample Output 0\n49\nSample Input 1\n3 10\nA\nC\nG\nSample Output 1\n1",
