  "text": "The High-\nDimensional Walsh-\nHadamard Transform\nYou are given two arrays A and B of length N = 2^D, indexed from 0 to N-1. Compute the XOR\nconvolution array C of length N, defined as: C[k] = sum_{i XOR j = k} (A[i] * B[j]) mod 998,244,353.\nPrint the XOR hash sum: sum_{k=0}^{N-1} (C[k] XOR k) mod 998,244,353\nInput Format\nLine 1: D (where N = 2^D, D <= 18) Line 2: A_0..A_{N-1} Line 3: B_0..B_{N-1}\nSample Input 0 2 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\nConstraints\n1 <= D <= 18 (N = 2^D up to 262,144)\n0 <= A[i], B[i] < 998,244,353\nOutput Format\nPrint the XOR hash sum modulo 998,244,353.\nSample Output 0 206",
